hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1645","\n Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Abu Bishr al-Wasiti narrated to us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us. Al-Dawraqi said: Yunus informed us. Abu Bishr said: From Yunus, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Amr ibn Wahb informed me, saying: I heard Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (RA) say: \There are two matters about which I will not ask anyone after having witnessed the Messenger of Allah"""""
"1646","\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Ayli – Mu'awiyah ibn 'Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah ibn 'Asim ibn al-Mundhir ibn az-Zubayr (in wording): Abu al-Mundhir Salam al-Qari narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Rafi', on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said:\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “When the prayer is about to begin, proceed to it while maintaining tranquility and dignity. Pray whatever you catch up with, and complete whatever you have missed.”"
